    {
      "category": "METHOD",
      "kind": "weapons permitted for black bear",
      "officialName": null,
      "state": "PROHIBITED",
      "statedAs": {
        "text": "(1) A person commits an offence where the person hunts (u) big game, other than bison, caribou, elk, grizzly bear, moose, mountain sheep or mountain goat, with a weapon other than a bow, muzzleloader, rifle or shotgun,",
        "lang": "en-CA"
      },
      "citation": "s. 17 (1) (u)",
      "scope": {
        "speciesIds": [
          "species:american-black-bear"
        ],
        "animalClass": null,
        "geography": {
          "kind": "JURISDICTION",
          "designations": [
            "BC"
          ],
          "statedAs": null
        },
        "seasonSegment": null,
        "methods": [
          "a weapon other than a bow, muzzleloader, rifle or shotgun"
        ],
        "dates": null,
        "hunterClass": {
          "residency": null,
          "age": null,
          "licenceType": null
        }
      },
      "unresolved": [
        "This row prohibits weapons OTHER than bow, muzzleloader, rifle or shotgun for black bear. It is not a statement that those four are ALLOWED without condition: s. 17 (1) (a), (b), (e), (h), (k), (l), (s), (t) and (v) each still restrict them.",
        "Whether an air rifle is a 'rifle' for s. 17 (1) (u) is not settled by the text read: s. 17 (1) (v) separately prohibits black bear 'with an air rifle that is less than .35 calibre', which implies an air rifle of .35 calibre or more is contemplated, but no provision read says so. Left unresolved."
      ]
    },
